window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_c-56fe4b8c0557eaf0"]={"key":"ny_c-56fe4b8c0557eaf0","group":"ny_c","uid":"56fe4b8c0557eaf0","rank":45,"title":"crownridge spoof front desk briefing","occupation":"software_developers","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_c1","prompt":"You are the site-coordination lead supporting Crownridge Health Network's 31 clinic front desks. Over the weekend, appointment-reminder emails were spoofed after Hawthorne Supply widened the SPF record used by the messaging service and left DKIM unsigned, and Ana Vanterpool needs something usable before Monday at 7am because coordinators are already taking patient calls. Work from `incident_messages.docx` and `mailing_log.xlsx` and create `crownridge_front_desk_briefing.docx` in the top level of the working directory. The file should be a front-desk briefing note for clinic site coordinators with a clear purpose and deadline, followed by a per-scenario action table that lets a non-technical coordinator decide what is genuine enough to act on, what to say to a patient, what to stop doing, and when and how to escalate. Keep the language calm, plain, and suitable for reading aloud; make each action explicit rather than relying on technical terms or vague instructions. Preserve the distinctions in the supplied messages and log, including cases involving a suspicious sender, a reply-to address, a link or payment request, a patient who has already interacted with a message, and a message that is not an appointment reminder. Include a short source-handling note that makes any necessary treatment of the supplied log's inconsistent dates, noisy rate value, and row-level notes visible without turning those source defects into patient-facing claims. Do not add advice that the sources do not support, do not tell staff to use a browser padlock as proof of authenticity, and do not ask patients to disclose credentials or payment details. Keep the briefing to three pages or fewer, use readable table text, and write the finished file as `crownridge_front_desk_briefing.docx` at the working-directory top level.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/incident_messages.docx` — Contains the source emails and interview-style notes from Ana Vanterpool, Antoni Hutchins, Marisol Mikkelsen, Magda Seaborne, and Gitta Lombardi describing the spoofing incident, supported authenticity signals, patient-facing language, escalation handling, and out-of-scope communications.\n- `references/mailing_log.xlsx` — Contains the supplied scenario records used to verify the per-scenario action table. It includes sender and reply-to observations, message content indicators, operational status, dates, a vendor rate field, and row-level notes that qualify or override the main columns.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `crownridge_front_desk_briefing.docx` — A polished front-desk briefing note with a per-scenario action table and a concise source-handling note. (Write the file into the top level of the working directory using exactly this filename.; Use three pages or fewer.; Use plain language appropriate for non-technical clinic site coordinators.; The action table must make the decision, patient wording, prohibited action, and escalation path explicit for every supplied scenario.; Do not introduce unsupported technical or patient-security claims.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/incident_messages.docx","bytes":38644,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/9d5223b3ab742142aa390a7e67ffc2aa5426ee5703fbabb42d43becf984d1bc6.docx","sha256":"9d5223b3ab742142aa390a7e67ffc2aa5426ee5703fbabb42d43becf984d1bc6","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"CROWNRIDGE HEALTH NETWORK\nWeekend appointment-reminder incident notes\nCompiled Sunday evening for Monday front-desk coordination\nAna Vanterpool | Messaging service owner\nOver the weekend, appointment-reminder emails were spoofed. Hawthorne Supply widened the SPF record used by the messaging service, and DKIM was left unsigned. We are receiving patient calls across the 31 clinic front desks. Use the Crownridge messaging incident channel for suspicious-message reports; I am the owner contact for the incident.\nMagda Seaborne | Security liaison\nThe visible sender address can be forged. It is not enough by itself to decide that a reminder is genuine. A browser padlock or an HTTPS appearance is not a test that the email itself is authentic. In the cases provided, a Crownridge reply-to can support other information, but it is not proof by itself.\nMarisol Mikkelsen | Scheduling-system contact\nFor appointment questions, check Crownridge's internal scheduling record. The record is how staff should verify appointment information. Do not turn a caller into a technical verifier of the email.\nAntoni Hutchins | Front-desk operations\nSuggested call language: “We are aware of misleading appointment-reminder messages. I can check your appointment information in our scheduling record.” Do not ask callers to read credentials, payment-card information, or one-time codes. Do not direct a caller to a phone number, link, or reply destination supplied only by a suspicious message.\nAna Vanterpool | Messaging service owner\nWhen a patient clicked or replied to a suspicious message, stop further interaction with that message. Do not request or repeat sensitive information. Record the report through the messaging incident channel and preserve the original message or a screenshot when available. Do not forward suspicious content to patients. This report does not establish that an account or identity was compromised.\nGitta Lombardi | Vendor liaison\nA Hawthorne Supply communication about marketing operations or invoicing is not a patient appointment-reminder message. It is outside the front-desk patient-response workflow; do not treat every Hawthorne Supply communication as a patient spoof.\nWorking distinction: message authenticity signals and appointment verification are different questions. A plausible sender or reply-to never replaces checking the internal scheduling record.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/mailing_log.xlsx","bytes":6576,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/427049af96cd548019630966ed3040f149364402ed9f6ed04960a7f8153047d1.xlsx","sha256":"427049af96cd548019630966ed3040f149364402ed9f6ed04960a7f8153047d1","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Mailing log","row_count":10,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Messaging service observations"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Weekend intake export - clinic coordinator queue"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Scenario","Received date/time","Visible sender","Reply-to observed","Message indicator","Scheduling record","Main action label","Vendor rate","Notes","Queue ref"]},{"r":"5","cells":["A","46257.34375","appointments@crownridgehealth.org","reminders@crownridgehealth.org","Appointment details; no payment or credential request","Matches internal appointment record","Routine reminder","0.075","No exception recorded.","CR-4817"]},{"r":"6","cells":["B","24/08/2026 09:40","appointments@crownridgehealth.org","notice@crownridge-care-mail.com","Unfamiliar link requests appointment action","No match checked at intake","Routine reminder","0.075","Visible Crownridge sender is not sufficient; non-Crownridge reply-to and unfamiliar link require suspicious handling.","CR-4821"]},{"r":"7","cells":["C","2026-08-24T10:05:00","appointments@crownridgehealth.org","reminders@crownridgehealth.org","Requests payment card details and sign-in credentials","Appointment may be referenced","Call patient back","0.07500000000000001","OVERRIDE: Treat as suspicious; do not act on a payment or credential request even when the sender appears to be Crownridge.","CR-4825"]},{"r":"8","cells":["D","2026-08-24T10:22:00","appointments@crownridgehealth.org","notice@crownridge-care-mail.com","Patient reports clicking link or replying","Check record for appointment questions","Routine call close","0.075","OVERRIDE: Already interacted. Stop further interaction and use the messaging incident channel.","CR-4828"]},{"r":"9","cells":["E","2026-08-24T11:10:00","billing@hawthornesupply.co","ar@hawthornesupply.co","Marketing operations invoice","Not applicable","Route to coordinator","0.07500000000000001","OVERRIDE: Vendor-facing Hawthorne Supply operation/invoice item; out of scope for the front-desk patient workflow.","CR-4830"]},{"r":"10","cells":["F","2026-08-24 12:35","appointments@crownridgehealth.org","reminders@crownridgehealth.org","Reminder wording; no payment request","Insufficient appointment corroboration in internal record","Routine reminder","0.075","Reply-to is a supporting signal only. Do not declare genuine without appointment corroboration.","CR-4834"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Exported 2026-08-24 18:42 UTC"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/crownridge_front_desk_briefing.docx","bytes":40600,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/2f12595e8e34764d31187237e0a2f22cef4ba707933c04c3268005086d4521b3.docx","sha256":"2f12595e8e34764d31187237e0a2f22cef4ba707933c04c3268005086d4521b3","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Front-Desk Briefing: Appointment-Reminder Calls\nCrownridge Health Network | For clinic site coordinators and front-desk staff | Use for calls before Monday, 7:00 a.m.\nPurpose. Give patients a calm, consistent response after weekend spoofed appointment-reminder emails. Ana Vanterpool, messaging-service owner, is the incident contact. The visible sender address can be forged; a Crownridge reply-to is only a supporting signal. Neither proves a message is genuine. Check appointment information in Crownridge's internal scheduling record.\nVERIFY\nUse the internal scheduling record for appointment questions. Do not ask a patient to validate the email.\nDO NOT USE AS PROOF\nA browser padlock or HTTPS appearance is not proof that the email is authentic.\nESCALATE\nPreserve the original message or screenshot when available. Send the report to Ana Vanterpool through the Crownridge messaging incident channel; do not forward suspicious content to patients.\n\nScenario actions\nIncoming situation / trigger\nDecision\nSay to the patient\nStop doing\nEscalate / next step\nA. Routine reminder: Crownridge-looking sender and Crownridge reply-to; appointment details match the internal scheduling record; no payment or credential request.\nRoutine reminder after record check.\n“I can confirm the appointment information in our scheduling record.”\nDo not rely on the sender or reply-to alone; do not ask the patient to prove the email is real.\nAnswer appointment questions from the internal record. No incident escalation is needed for this corroborated case.\nB. Unfamiliar link and non-Crownridge reply-to, even though the visible sender looks like Crownridge.\nSuspicious. Do not act through the message.\n“We are aware of misleading reminders. I can check your appointment in our scheduling record.”\nDo not open or recommend the unfamiliar link, reply, or use a phone number supplied only in this message.\nKeep the original or a screenshot when available; report through the Crownridge messaging incident channel to Ana Vanterpool.\nC. Message appears from Crownridge but asks for payment, credentials, or a one-time code.\nSuspicious.\n“Please do not share payment or sign-in information from that message. I can check the appointment in our scheduling record.”\nDo not request or repeat credentials, payment-card information, or one-time codes. Do not take payment through the message.\nPreserve message/screenshot when available; report through the Crownridge messaging incident channel to Ana Vanterpool.\nD. Patient already clicked a link or replied to a suspicious reminder.\nAlready interacted: use incident response.\n“Please stop using that message. I can check your appointment in our scheduling record.”\nStop further clicking, replying, payment, or information exchange. Do not request or repeat credentials, payment-card information, or one-time codes.\nPreserve message/screenshot when available; record the report through the Crownridge messaging incident channel to Ana Vanterpool. Do not state that an account or identity was compromised.\nE. Hawthorne Supply marketing operations or invoice communication; not an appointment reminder.\nOut of scope for patient workflow.\nNo patient wording: this is not a patient appointment-reminder call.\nDo not convert this vendor item into a reminder response or tell patients it is a spoof.\nHandle outside the front-desk patient workflow; it is not the same response for every Hawthorne Supply communication.\nF. Crownridge reply-to, but appointment details are not sufficiently corroborated in the internal scheduling record.\nDo not declare genuine; treat cautiously and escalate.\n“I cannot confirm that message. I can check your appointment in our scheduling record.”\nDo not treat the reply-to as proof. Do not direct the patient to the message link, reply destination, or any supplied phone number.\nPreserve message/screenshot when available; report through the Crownridge messaging incident channel to Ana Vanterpool while using the internal record for appointment questions.\nSource-handling note. This briefing applied row-level Notes as overrides to the log’s main columns. The date/time column mixes an ISO-style timestamp with a slash-separated date/time, so no exact chronology is inferred beyond the weekend-to-Monday context. The vendor-rate field includes insignificant floating-point decimal noise; it is source metadata, not a patient fee, threshold, or authenticity test.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"r01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted artifact is a readable DOCX file.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"File type and successful document extraction.","grader_hint":"Open or parse the submitted file as an Office Open XML document."},{"rubric_item_id":"r02","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Crownridge Health Network.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible document text.","grader_hint":"Search extracted text for the exact organisation name."},{"rubric_item_id":"r03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document identifies Ana Vanterpool as the messaging-service or incident owner.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible document text.","grader_hint":"Check the opening note or escalation guidance."},{"rubric_item_id":"r04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document is explicitly addressed to clinic site coordinators or front-desk staff.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Title, audience statement, or table language.","grader_hint":"Confirm the intended audience is visible without relying on filename."},{"rubric_item_id":"r05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Monday 7am operational deadline is stated or clearly preserved.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening context or deadline statement.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent wording that preserves the deadline."},{"rubric_item_id":"r06","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document contains a per-scenario action table covering all six supplied scenario meanings.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Table rows mapped to source scenario identifiers or unmistakable descriptions.","grader_hint":"Match each row to scenarios A-F from mailing_log.xlsx; merged rows count only if every scenario remains separately actionable."},{"rubric_item_id":"r07","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The action table gives a clear decision or disposition for every covered scenario.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision/status column or equivalent prose.","grader_hint":"Each scenario must say whether staff may treat it as a routine reminder, should treat it as suspicious, should escalate, or is out of scope."},{"rubric_item_id":"r08","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The action table gives patient-facing wording or a concrete sentence to say for every patient-facing scenario.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Say-to-patient column or equivalent row text.","grader_hint":"Do not award for generic advice outside the row; each applicable row needs usable wording."},{"rubric_item_id":"r09","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The action table gives an explicit stop-doing instruction for every suspicious or already-interacted scenario.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Stop or do-not column or equivalent row text.","grader_hint":"Look for prohibited interaction with links, replies, payment requests, credentials, or supplied phone numbers as applicable."},{"rubric_item_id":"r10","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The action table gives an escalation outcome for suspicious and already-interacted scenarios.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Escalation column or row instructions.","grader_hint":"The route must identify Ana Vanterpool or the supplied Crownridge messaging incident channel."},{"rubric_item_id":"r11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing states that a visible sender address can be forged.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible plain-language statement.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent wording such as sender display or from-address is not proof."},{"rubric_item_id":"r12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing does not treat the visible sender address alone as proof of authenticity.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Combined statement and scenario decisions.","grader_hint":"A sender matching Crownridge must still be corroborated or handled cautiously."},{"rubric_item_id":"r13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The routine corroborated reminder is not rejected solely because its visible sender could be forged.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario A row.","grader_hint":"The row should use the internal appointment record and supplied supporting signals rather than a blanket rejection."},{"rubric_item_id":"r14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document treats the Crownridge reply-to as a supporting signal rather than standalone proof.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"General guidance and scenario F.","grader_hint":"Check that reply-to is neither ignored in all cases nor elevated to sufficient authentication."},{"rubric_item_id":"r15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document does not declare scenario F genuine solely because its reply-to belongs to Crownridge.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario F row.","grader_hint":"The missing appointment corroboration must lead to caution or escalation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r16","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing directs staff to verify appointment information using Crownridge's internal scheduling record.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible instructions or patient wording.","grader_hint":"Equivalent wording referring to the internal scheduling system is acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"r17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing does not direct patients to use a phone number supplied only by a suspicious message.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Suspicious-message rows.","grader_hint":"Check both patient wording and stop-doing instructions."},{"rubric_item_id":"r18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing does not direct patients to follow an unfamiliar link from the suspicious message.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario B row and general guidance.","grader_hint":"The document may tell staff not to use or recommend the link; it must not endorse it."},{"rubric_item_id":"r19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing tells staff not to request or repeat credentials, payment-card information, or one-time codes.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario C and patient-language sections.","grader_hint":"All three sensitive-information categories should be covered or clearly encompassed."},{"rubric_item_id":"r20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The payment-or-credential scenario is classified as suspicious even if the message appears to come from Crownridge.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario C row.","grader_hint":"The suspicious classification must not depend only on the sender field."},{"rubric_item_id":"r21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing states that a browser padlock or HTTPS appearance is not proof that the email is authentic.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible warning or scenario guidance.","grader_hint":"Accept plain-language equivalents."},{"rubric_item_id":"r22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The already-clicked-or-replied scenario tells staff to stop further interaction with the suspicious message.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario D row.","grader_hint":"Look for no further clicking, replying, payment, or credential exchange."},{"rubric_item_id":"r23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The already-clicked-or-replied scenario directs staff to use the supplied internal escalation route.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario D row.","grader_hint":"Ana Vanterpool or the Crownridge messaging incident channel must be named."},{"rubric_item_id":"r24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The already-interacted guidance does not assert that the patient's account or identity was compromised.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario D wording.","grader_hint":"The source supports escalation and caution, not a confirmed compromise."},{"rubric_item_id":"r25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing tells staff to preserve the original suspicious message or a screenshot when available.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Escalation instructions.","grader_hint":"Equivalent evidence-preservation wording is acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"r26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Hawthorne Supply vendor or invoice communication is identified as outside the patient appointment-reminder workflow.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario E row.","grader_hint":"It must be excluded from patient-facing action rather than converted into a reminder response."},{"rubric_item_id":"r27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing does not claim that every Hawthorne Supply communication is a patient spoof or requires the same front-desk response.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope wording and scenario E row.","grader_hint":"The source distinguishes vendor operations from patient reminders."},{"rubric_item_id":"r28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The routine corroborated scenario directs staff to use the internal record for appointment questions rather than asking the patient to validate the email technically.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario A row.","grader_hint":"Award only when the operational action is clear."},{"rubric_item_id":"r29","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The suspicious-link scenario identifies both the unfamiliar link and the non-Crownridge reply-to as reasons not to act through the message.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario B row.","grader_hint":"Both source distinctions should survive the restructuring."},{"rubric_item_id":"r30","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each scenario row names or unmistakably describes the relevant trigger, rather than using generic labels such as 'Case 1' with no explanation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scenario table text.","grader_hint":"A coordinator must be able to match the row to the incoming situation."},{"rubric_item_id":"r31","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document acknowledges that row-level Notes override the corresponding main-column information in the supplied log.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source-handling note.","grader_hint":"The statement must refer to the Notes or row-level exception field."},{"rubric_item_id":"r32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The final classifications follow the Notes overrides for the payment/credential case, the already-interacted case, and the out-of-scope vendor case.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison of briefing rows with Notes in mailing_log.xlsx.","grader_hint":"Check all three override-bearing scenarios independently."},{"rubric_item_id":"r33","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The source-handling note acknowledges that the date/time column contains mixed representations.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible note in the DOCX.","grader_hint":"The note need not reproduce every source date."},{"rubric_item_id":"r34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing does not present an unsupported exact chronology derived from the ambiguous slash-separated date.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timeline wording and source-handling note.","grader_hint":"General weekend-to-Monday context is supported; false precision about the ambiguous record is not."},{"rubric_item_id":"r35","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The source-handling note acknowledges the noisy floating-point representation in the supplied rate field.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Visible note in the DOCX.","grader_hint":"Accept wording about insignificant decimal or floating-point noise."},{"rubric_item_id":"r36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing does not turn the noisy vendor-rate field into an unsupported patient-facing fee, threshold, or authenticity test.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole document and source-handling note.","grader_hint":"The rate is source metadata, not a basis for telling patients what to do."},{"rubric_item_id":"r37","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document preserves the distinction between message authenticity and appointment verification.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"General guidance plus scenarios A and F.","grader_hint":"A technically plausible signal must not replace checking the internal scheduling record."},{"rubric_item_id":"r38","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The escalation guidance is operationally complete enough for a coordinator to know what to retain, whom to contact, and what not to send to a patient.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Escalation section and relevant table rows.","grader_hint":"Require evidence preservation, supplied internal route, and no forwarding of suspicious content to patients."},{"rubric_item_id":"r39","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A non-technical coordinator could use the briefing correctly on first reading: decisions are unambiguous, patient wording is calm and usable, and no material supplied scenario is left for improvisation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document reviewed as a whole.","grader_hint":"Judge practical usability, clarity, and completeness rather than merely counting headings or rows."},{"rubric_item_id":"r40","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing remains faithful to the supplied material and does not invent legal, clinical, account-compromise, or technical claims.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole-document comparison against both references.","grader_hint":"Penalize unsupported additions that could change front-desk behaviour even if they sound security-conscious."},{"rubric_item_id":"r41","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered DOCX contains no #REF!, #DIV/0!, or #VALUE! error strings.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Extracted document XML and rendered text.","grader_hint":"Search all document text and table cells."},{"rubric_item_id":"r42","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document is no more than three pages and remains readable when rendered.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX page count and visual inspection.","grader_hint":"Do not award if the table is technically present but clipped, unreadable, or spills beyond three pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"r43","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The briefing instructs staff to use the browser padlock, HTTPS appearance, or a similar browser indicator as proof of authenticity.","weight":-5.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole-document search and rendered review.","grader_hint":"Apply once if the document recommends or implies that the padlock/HTTPS proves the email is genuine; do not penalize a clear warning that it is not proof."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Crownridge Health Network is responding to a patient-facing email spoofing incident involving its appointment-reminder service and the Hawthorne Supply marketing vendor. Ana Vanterpool needs a concise briefing that clinic site coordinators can use consistently before the Monday morning operational deadline.","difficulty_sources":["Translate technical email-authentication evidence into safe, unambiguous front-desk language","Preserve scenario-specific exceptions from messy source records","Distinguish supported actions from plausible but unsupported security advice","Handle mixed date representations and floating-point rate noise without creating false precision"],"authoring_plan":{"source_set":{"files":["incident_messages.docx","mailing_log.xlsx"],"semantic_relationship":"The DOCX supplies the narrative and stakeholder guidance; the XLSX supplies the scenario-level observations. The gold briefing is a faithful restructuring of both sources, with row-level Notes taking precedence over conflicting main-column labels.","no_other_seeded_defects":true},"incident_messages_content":{"incident_summary":"Ana Vanterpool's messaging service was spoofed over the weekend. Hawthorne Supply widened the SPF record used for the service and DKIM was left unsigned. The incident caused patient calls to 31 clinic front desks.","supported_authenticity_interpretation":["The visible sender address can be forged and is not sufficient proof that an appointment reminder is genuine.","A reply-to address belonging to Crownridge is a useful supporting signal in the supplied cases, but it is not a reason to ask a patient to reveal information.","A browser padlock or HTTPS appearance is not an authentication test for the message and must not be presented as proof.","A message that asks for credentials, payment details, or an unfamiliar link is not to be acted on as an appointment reminder."],"patient_language":["Tell a caller that staff are aware of misleading appointment-reminder messages and will verify appointment information through Crownridge's internal scheduling record.","Do not ask the caller to read credentials, payment-card information, or one-time codes to the front desk.","Do not direct a caller to use a phone number, link, or reply destination supplied only by the suspicious message."],"already_interacted_case":["If a patient clicked or replied to a suspicious message, staff should stop further interaction with that message, avoid requesting or repeating sensitive information, record the incident through the supplied internal escalation route, and tell the patient that the clinic will use the verified scheduling record for appointment questions.","The briefing must not claim that a patient account was compromised unless the source states that fact."],"scope_case":["A Hawthorne Supply vendor communication about marketing operations or invoicing is not an appointment-reminder message and is outside the front-desk patient response workflow.","The briefing should identify that case as out of scope rather than converting it into a patient instruction."],"escalation":"The supplied notes identify Ana Vanterpool and the Crownridge messaging incident channel as the escalation route. The coordinator should preserve the original message or screenshot when available and avoid forwarding suspicious content to patients.","stakeholder_roles":{"Ana Vanterpool":"Messaging-service owner and incident escalation contact.","Antoni Hutchins":"Front-desk operations contact who supplied the coordinator-facing call language.","Marisol Mikkelsen":"Scheduling-system contact who confirmed that appointment details should be checked in the internal record.","Magda Seaborne":"Security liaison who supplied the warning about forged sender addresses and the invalidity of the padlock test.","Gitta Lombardi":"Vendor liaison who identified Hawthorne Supply communications as outside the patient-reminder workflow."}},"mailing_log_semantics":{"scenario_records":[{"scenario":"A","meaning":"A routine appointment reminder whose visible sender resembles Crownridge, whose reply-to is the supplied Crownridge address, whose appointment details match the internal scheduling record, and which contains no payment or credential request.","notes_effect":"No exception; use the main fields."},{"scenario":"B","meaning":"A message with a forged-looking Crownridge sender and a non-Crownridge reply-to that asks the recipient to use an unfamiliar link.","notes_effect":"No exception; classify as suspicious and do not direct the patient to the link."},{"scenario":"C","meaning":"A message that appears to come from Crownridge but asks for payment or credentials.","notes_effect":"The Notes field overrides the main action label and requires the message to be treated as suspicious."},{"scenario":"D","meaning":"A patient reports clicking or replying to a suspicious reminder.","notes_effect":"The Notes field overrides the ordinary response field and requires the already-interacted escalation response."},{"scenario":"E","meaning":"A vendor-facing Hawthorne Supply operational or invoice communication that is not an appointment reminder.","notes_effect":"The Notes field marks it out of scope for the front-desk patient workflow even if the main columns make it look actionable."},{"scenario":"F","meaning":"A message with a Crownridge reply-to but insufficient appointment corroboration in the internal scheduling record.","notes_effect":"No exception; it must not be declared genuine solely from the reply-to address."}],"defects":["The Notes column contains row-level exceptions that override the corresponding main action or classification columns; the exceptions occur in more than one scenario.","The vendor-rate field contains a floating-point representation with insignificant binary-style noise rather than an exact decimal equality.","The single date/time column mixes an unambiguous ISO-style timestamp with a slash-separated day/month value whose interpretation is ambiguous without the narrative context."],"data_integrity":"All substantive scenario facts are complete and mutually consistent after applying the row-level Notes overrides. There are no duplicate records, formula errors, missing required values, zero denominators, hidden images, or additional seeded defects."},"gold_transformation":{"operation":"Restructure the supplied narrative and scenario records into a concise DOCX briefing. Preserve supported facts, consolidate repeated guidance, and express each scenario as an explicit coordinator decision with patient wording, stop-doing instruction, and escalation outcome.","required_disclosures":["State that the visible sender address can be forged.","State that a Crownridge reply-to is only a supporting signal and does not justify requesting sensitive information.","State that the browser padlock is not proof of message authenticity.","State that row-level Notes override the main columns.","Acknowledge the mixed date representation and explain the conservative treatment used for the briefing timeline.","Acknowledge the floating-point rate noise without presenting a falsely exact derived claim."],"required_scenario_coverage":["Routine corroborated reminder","Suspicious link and non-Crownridge reply-to","Payment or credential request","Patient who already clicked or replied","Out-of-scope Hawthorne Supply communication","Insufficiently corroborated reminder with a Crownridge reply-to"],"gold_quality":["A coordinator can choose an action on first reading without inferring missing steps.","Patient wording is calm and does not blame the patient.","The briefing does not tell staff to use the padlock, sender display, or reply-to alone as proof.","The briefing does not invent compromise, legal, clinical, or technical consequences not present in the sources."]}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"ref_incident_messages","filename":"incident_messages.docx","purpose":"Contains the source emails and interview-style notes from Ana Vanterpool, Antoni Hutchins, Marisol Mikkelsen, Magda Seaborne, and Gitta Lombardi describing the spoofing incident, supported authenticity signals, patient-facing language, escalation handling, and out-of-scope communications.","required":true,"discovery":"Read this file first for the authoritative wording and scenario context; compare it with the scenario records in mailing_log.xlsx."},{"artifact_id":"ref_mailing_log","filename":"mailing_log.xlsx","purpose":"Contains the supplied scenario records used to verify the per-scenario action table. It includes sender and reply-to observations, message content indicators, operational status, dates, a vendor rate field, and row-level notes that qualify or override the main columns.","required":true,"discovery":"Inspect the complete table, including the Notes column and all date/time values; do not rely only on the first visible rows."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"briefing_docx","filename":"crownridge_front_desk_briefing.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A polished front-desk briefing note with a per-scenario action table and a concise source-handling note.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file into the top level of the working directory using exactly this filename.","Use three pages or fewer.","Use plain language appropriate for non-technical clinic site coordinators.","The action table must make the decision, patient wording, prohibited action, and escalation path explicit for every supplied scenario.","Do not introduce unsupported technical or patient-security claims."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"analyze_data","work_product":"professional_report","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"software_developers","sector":"professional_scientific_technical_services","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":2.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Build the reference briefing from the supplied semantic source specification, then have an independent reviewer compare every scenario row and every security claim against both reference files and review the rendered document for first-read usability.","minimum_reviewers":1,"known_limitations":["The exact visual layout and wording may vary, but the six scenario dispositions and source-handling disclosures must remain traceable.","The supplied rate field is intentionally irrelevant to patient action; grading checks that it is handled transparently rather than requiring it to appear in the briefing."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"结构/材料验收记录","detail":"validated 属于结构、防泄漏、材料推进验收；没有内容正确率结论。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T02:33:29+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T02:33:29+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T02:33:29+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T02:33:29+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T02:33:29+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_c1/runs/56fe4b8c0557eaf0","declared_deliverables":["crownridge_front_desk_briefing.docx"]};
